        "reported_material_gaps": [],
        "research_rationale": "Identity: the held Federal Register text is Executive Order 9949 modifying Executive Order 9721 for Paul D. Miles (read in full). Inventory read and confirmed: one clause, the whole operative text. End: express revocation by Executive Order 12553 on 1986-02-25 naming the order by number. Whether Mr. Miles in fact transferred, and whether any reemployment right accrued, is not established by any held source and is not needed for the end, because the end rests on an express revocation, not on exhaustion; any accrued reemployment right is a surviving consequence that this claim does not assert or deny. Prior research: none reported. Searches: current-law:usc, current-law:ecfr, later-events:ofr_catalog, all complete with no coverage warning.\nMember checks: {\"earlier_end_check\":\"The order has no fixed end date or termination clause. Its five-year window (later amended to December 31, 1953 by Executive Order 10415) is a condition on the employee's reemployment rights, not an end date of the order. The one-person modification may have been exhausted by performance, but no held source shows that the transfer occurred, so no exhaustion date is claimed. The dossier's chain, its three selected machine searches and my reading of Executive Order 12553 show no earlier revoking or superseding instrument; the only earlier event is the Executive Order 10415 amendment, recorded as a later event.\",\"independent_command_check\":\"The order contains one command, the person-specific modification. It does not create a regulation, delegation or standing rule. The underlying rule in paragraph 3(a) of Executive Order 9721 is a separate command of that order, which Executive Order 12553 also lists as revoked.\",\"savings_check\":\"Executive Order 12553 was read in full; it has no saving clause. No exhaustion or accrual is shown by held sources. Savings state none_after_bounded_search with the qualification stated in the savings reason.\",\"scope_check\":\"One clause is inventoried: the whole order, a single modification of paragraph 3(a) of Executive Order 9721 for one named employee, plus the direction to publish. Executive Order 12553 revokes the order by number as a whole.\"}",
